+\subsection{Canonized single-modulus core-envelope gate}
+\label{subsec:rt_canonized_single_modulus_core_gate}
+
+\textbf{[CANON LEMMA IMPORTED FROM MAIN CANON].}
+The main canon now accepts the local resolved core-envelope lemma
+\begin{equation}
+    E_\perp[\Psi]
+    =
+    \kappa\int_{\mathbb R^2}
+    \left[
+        |\nabla\Psi|^2
+        +\frac{1}{2\xi^2}(1-|\Psi|^2)^2
+    \right]d^2x,
+    \qquad
+    \Psi(\rho,\theta)=F(\rho)e^{in\theta}.
+\end{equation}
+The lemma canonizes a single isotropic stiffness modulus for the internal
+transverse core-envelope layer.  After \(\rho=\xi r\), this gives
+\begin{equation}
+    \mathcal L_r
+    =
+    F'^2r+n^2\frac{F^2}{r}+\frac12(F^2-1)^2r .
+\end{equation}
+Equivalently, in the generic notation
+\begin{equation}
+    \mathcal L_r
+    =A F'^2r+B n^2\frac{F^2}{r}+\frac{C}{2}(F^2-1)^2r,
+\end{equation}
+one has
+\begin{equation}
+    \boxed{A=B=C.}
+\end{equation}
+For the unit vortex sector, the radial core equation is therefore
+\begin{equation}
+    F''+\frac{F'}{r}-\frac{F}{r^2}+F(1-F^2)=0.
+\end{equation}
+Thus the GP/NLSE equation used by the Track B ring-constant extraction is now
+canon-derived from the local SST core-envelope lemma, rather than imported as
+an external effective model.  The v10B.0 coefficient \(\frac14(F^2-1)^2r\) is
+rejected for this unit convention; it would generate a depletion coefficient
+\(C/A=1/2\) instead of unity.
+
+\textbf{[CANON BOUNDARY].}
+This closes the internal core-envelope gate only.  It does not identify the
+core sound speed with the causal speed \(c\), nor does it prove the open
+core--torsion impedance identity required for the Lorentz-compatible
+Swirl-Clock.  Numerical values such as
+\(\alpha_{\rm ring}^{\rm GP}\approx1.61935\) remain ring-constant extraction
+results whose asymptotic and numerical status is documented separately.
